WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.940
Two dials, both labelled t.

2
00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:04.820
One sets a point's x.

3
00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.850
The other sets its y.

4
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:11.280
Turn t, and the readouts
tick: x equals cos t,

5
00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:13.310
y equals sine t.

6
00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.700
Somewhere, a point is moving.

7
00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.590
But its trail is hidden.

8
00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.240
What shape is it tracing?

9
00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:20.260
A sine wave?

10
00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:21.580
A straight line?

11
00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.500
And how fast is it going?

12
00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:28.320
In this mission, you'll see how a parameter
gives exactly one point for each value

13
00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:29.390
of t.

14
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.680
You'll eliminate the parameter, turning
the pair of equations into one Cartesian

15
00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:34.770
equation.

16
00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:39.560
And you'll see how the domain of t
decides which part of a curve is drawn.

17
00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:42.640
Your mission: find the
shape this point traces,

18
00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:44.280
and how fast it moves.
